1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,356
The COE: Paying for
Permission to Own a Car,

2
00:00:03,436 --> 00:00:05,700
Then Paying Again to Drive It

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,525
The gantries are coming down.

4
00:00:08,525 --> 00:00:11,997
Since October 2026, work
crews have been unbolting

5
00:00:12,077 --> 00:00:15,549
the grey-blue frames that
have spanned Singapore's

6
00:00:15,629 --> 00:00:18,817
expressways and city
streets for a generation,

7
00:00:18,897 --> 00:00:22,875
and by the middle of November
a dozen were already gone.

8
00:00:22,875 --> 00:00:27,340
The last working gantries will
go on charging until the 31st

9
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:31,658
of December 2026; from the
1st of January 2027 the charge

10
00:00:31,738 --> 00:00:35,975
arrives by satellite instead,
and the sign that a charged

11
00:00:36,055 --> 00:00:40,600
road lies ahead will be an oval
of blue paint on the tarmac.

12
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,850
It is the end of the most
visible piece of a system

13
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:47,375
that does something no other
country attempts in quite

14
00:00:47,455 --> 00:00:50,835
the same way: it makes a
driver pay for permission to

15
00:00:50,915 --> 00:00:54,375
own a car, and then pay
again, per trip, to drive it.

16
00:00:54,375 --> 00:00:56,906
The two charges have different names,

17
00:00:56,986 --> 00:00:59,950
different histories and one shared reason.

18
00:00:59,950 --> 00:01:02,600
This is the story of both.

19
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:07,170
Singapore began pricing congestion
earlier than anywhere else,

20
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:10,025
and with almost no technology at all.

21
00:01:10,025 --> 00:01:14,482
On the 2nd of June 1975 the Area
Licensing Scheme (ALS) began:

22
00:01:14,562 --> 00:01:19,019
to drive into a Restricted Zone
of about 6.7 square kilometres

23
00:01:19,099 --> 00:01:22,459
around the city centre
during the morning peak,

24
00:01:22,539 --> 00:01:26,996
a motorist bought a paper licence
— 3 Singapore dollars a day,

25
00:01:27,076 --> 00:01:32,125
or 60 Singapore dollars a month —
and displayed it on the windscreen.

26
00:01:32,125 --> 00:01:36,300
Police at the zone's entry
points checked for it by eye.

27
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:42,715
It was the world's first congestion-pricing
scheme put successfully into practice,

28
00:01:42,795 --> 00:01:45,012
and its effect was immediate:

29
00:01:45,092 --> 00:01:50,794
vehicles entering the zone between
7.30 and 9.30 in the morning fell from

30
00:01:50,874 --> 00:01:55,468
about 32,500 to about 7,700,
a drop of roughly 76 per cent,

31
00:01:55,548 --> 00:02:00,300
far beyond the 25 to 30 per
cent the planners had aimed for.

32
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:05,100
The scheme ran for 23 years,
but its limits were built in.

33
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:09,950
A monthly licence, once bought,
made every extra trip free.

34
00:02:09,950 --> 00:02:13,072
The charge could not
vary by time of day or by

35
00:02:13,152 --> 00:02:15,438
how crowded the road actually was,

36
00:02:15,518 --> 00:02:19,625
and enforcement meant a human
being looking at windscreens.

37
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:22,453
What the paper licence could never do was

38
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:25,300
price the driving itself, trip by trip.

39
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:29,525
That problem would eventually
be solved electronically.

40
00:02:29,525 --> 00:02:33,397
First, though, Singapore attacked
the other half of the question:

41
00:02:33,477 --> 00:02:37,550
not how much its cars were driven,
but how many of them there were.

42
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:41,371
Through the 1980s, rising
incomes put cars within

43
00:02:41,451 --> 00:02:45,510
reach of more and more
families, and by 1990 the car

44
00:02:45,590 --> 00:02:49,650
population was growing at
about 12 per cent a year.

45
00:02:49,650 --> 00:02:52,640
There were already some 280,000 cars,

46
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:57,450
and roads took up about 12
per cent of the island's land.

47
00:02:57,450 --> 00:03:01,143
A parliamentary select
committee on land transport

48
00:03:01,223 --> 00:03:05,520
recommended rationing the fleet
itself, and on the 27th of

49
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:09,600
February 1990 the Vehicle
Quota System was announced.

50
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:13,934
The first bidding exercise was
held on the 2nd of April 1990,

51
00:03:14,014 --> 00:03:16,828
and from the 1st of May that year nobody

52
00:03:16,908 --> 00:03:20,808
could register a car in
Singapore without first winning

53
00:03:20,888 --> 00:03:24,650
the right to: a Certificate
of Entitlement, the COE.

54
00:03:24,650 --> 00:03:27,825
The certificate is an auction product.

55
00:03:27,825 --> 00:03:31,699
The Land Transport Authority
(LTA) sets a quota for each period

56
00:03:31,779 --> 00:03:36,030
from a simple formula — the allowed
growth in the vehicle population,

57
00:03:36,110 --> 00:03:39,544
plus the number of vehicles
expected to be deregistered,

58
00:03:39,624 --> 00:03:43,059
plus adjustments — and motorists
and dealers bid for the

59
00:03:43,139 --> 00:03:47,515
certificates within categories, seven
at the start and five since 1999:

60
00:03:47,595 --> 00:03:50,653
A for smaller cars, B for
larger ones, C for goods

61
00:03:50,733 --> 00:03:54,750
vehicles and buses, D for
motorcycles, and E, the open category.

62
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:58,573
Bidding was a sealed tender
at first; open bidding,

63
00:03:58,653 --> 00:04:03,550
where everyone can watch the
current price, replaced it in 2001.

64
00:04:03,550 --> 00:04:06,525
A COE lasts ten years.

65
00:04:06,525 --> 00:04:11,531
At the end of the term the owner either
pays the Prevailing Quota Premium —

66
00:04:11,611 --> 00:04:16,211
a moving average of recent premiums
— to renew for five or ten years,

67
00:04:16,291 --> 00:04:20,144
or deregisters the car,
collecting a rebate of part of the

68
00:04:20,224 --> 00:04:24,700
car's Additional Registration Fee
that shrinks with the car's age.

69
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:27,382
The growth allowance inside the quota

70
00:04:27,462 --> 00:04:30,075
is where the long tightening shows.

71
00:04:30,075 --> 00:04:33,175
It began at 3 per cent a year.

72
00:04:33,175 --> 00:04:38,375
It was cut to 1.5 per cent
in 2009, 1 per cent in 2012,

73
00:04:38,455 --> 00:04:42,599
0.5 per cent in 2013,
0.25 per cent in 2015,

74
00:04:42,679 --> 00:04:48,838
and from February 2018 it has been
zero for cars and motorcycles:

75
00:04:48,918 --> 00:04:52,950
the fleet is not permitted to grow at all.

76
00:04:52,950 --> 00:04:57,575
Every new car on the road
replaces one that has left it.

77
00:04:57,575 --> 00:05:01,936
Because the supply of certificates
follows deregistrations —

78
00:05:02,016 --> 00:05:05,785
which bunch, ten years on,
behind past sales booms —

79
00:05:05,865 --> 00:05:10,750
the COE premium does not move like
a price so much as like a tide.

80
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:13,927
In December 1994, amid speculation,

81
00:05:14,007 --> 00:05:19,511
premiums broke 100,000 Singapore
dollars for the first time,

82
00:05:19,591 --> 00:05:25,175
the largest-car category reaching
110,500 Singapore dollars.

83
00:05:25,175 --> 00:05:28,838
In December 1997, as the
Asian financial crisis bit,

84
00:05:28,918 --> 00:05:33,733
one category's premium collapsed
from 64,100 Singapore dollars to 50

85
00:05:33,813 --> 00:05:37,836
Singapore dollars in a single
exercise; a doctor used his

86
00:05:37,916 --> 00:05:43,018
50 Singapore dollars certificate to
register a new Honda Integra Type R,

87
00:05:43,098 --> 00:05:47,769
and the transport minister of the
day called such results "flukes,

88
00:05:47,849 --> 00:05:50,800
aberrations" of the blind-bidding system.

89
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:54,860
In November 2008, after
the global financial crisis

90
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:59,567
and an over-estimate of
deregistrations flooded the quota,

91
00:05:59,647 --> 00:06:02,975
Category A closed at 2 Singapore dollars.

92
00:06:02,975 --> 00:06:06,300
The swings have not gentled with age.

93
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:10,522
On the 18th of October
2023, Category B set an

94
00:06:10,602 --> 00:06:15,011
all-time record of 150,001
Singapore dollars and

95
00:06:15,091 --> 00:06:19,219
the open category 158,004
Singapore dollars —

96
00:06:19,299 --> 00:06:23,975
the certificate alone
costing more than most cars.

97
00:06:23,975 --> 00:06:27,907
Three weeks later, with
a larger quota released,

98
00:06:27,987 --> 00:06:31,250
Category B fell 40,000 Singapore dollars

99
00:06:31,330 --> 00:06:35,175
in one exercise, the
steepest drop since 1995.

100
00:06:35,175 --> 00:06:39,698
Since 2023 the LTA has tried
to sand the edges off the cycle

101
00:06:39,778 --> 00:06:44,531
with a "cut-and-fill" adjustment,
bringing forward certificates

102
00:06:44,611 --> 00:06:48,600
from future deregistrations
to fatten lean quarters.

103
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:52,778
It has not flattened the tide:
on the 4th of November 2026,

104
00:06:52,858 --> 00:06:57,324
Category A reached 139,001
Singapore dollars, its highest ever,

105
00:06:57,404 --> 00:07:01,366
closing above Category B.
Singaporeans have long treated

106
00:07:01,446 --> 00:07:05,046
the cycle as folk wisdom
— buy in the trough years,

107
00:07:05,126 --> 00:07:10,250
hold through the peaks — and plan
their cars' ten-year lives around it.

108
00:07:10,250 --> 00:07:14,563
The paper licence's electronic
successor arrived on the

109
00:07:14,643 --> 00:07:18,797
1st of April 1998, when
Electronic Road Pricing (ERP)

110
00:07:18,877 --> 00:07:23,350
was switched on at two points
on the East Coast Parkway.

111
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:27,407
By September that year the
first phase was complete —

112
00:07:27,487 --> 00:07:31,623
33 gantries across the city
and the main expressways —

113
00:07:31,703 --> 00:07:34,825
and the last ALS gantries had come down.

114
00:07:34,825 --> 00:07:38,626
It was the world's first
electronic road-pricing

115
00:07:38,706 --> 00:07:41,536
system used for congestion charging,

116
00:07:41,616 --> 00:07:46,225
built at a capital cost of
197 million Singapore dollars.

117
00:07:46,225 --> 00:07:51,206
Every vehicle carried an In-vehicle
Unit with a stored-value CashCard;

118
00:07:51,286 --> 00:07:55,110
passing under a gantry debited
the card automatically,

119
00:07:55,190 --> 00:07:58,950
no stopping, no windscreen
licence, no one watching.

120
00:07:58,950 --> 00:08:02,113
Traffic responded as it had in 1975:

121
00:08:02,193 --> 00:08:08,510
expressway volumes fell by about 15
per cent, and average speeds in the

122
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:13,275
charged hours rose from 35
to 55 kilometres an hour.

123
00:08:13,275 --> 00:08:15,685
Unlike the flat paper licence,

124
00:08:15,765 --> 00:08:19,750
ERP prices each trip, and
prices it by evidence.

125
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:24,678
The LTA reviews rates every quarter
against target speed bands —

126
00:08:24,758 --> 00:08:28,747
45 to 65 kilometres an hour
on expressways, 20 to 30

127
00:08:28,827 --> 00:08:33,363
on city and arterial roads —
raising a charge where traffic

128
00:08:33,443 --> 00:08:37,825
runs too slowly and lowering
it where the road has room.

129
00:08:37,825 --> 00:08:41,073
Graduated rate steps, introduced in 2003,

130
00:08:41,153 --> 00:08:46,592
softened the cliff edges between
one half-hour's price and the next;

131
00:08:46,672 --> 00:08:50,000
evening-peak charging followed from 2005.

132
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:54,325
The network grew to more than
ninety charging locations.

133
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:58,265
Other cities came to learn:
London's congestion charge,

134
00:08:58,345 --> 00:09:04,185
launched in 2003, was modelled on Singapore's
system after its officials visited,

135
00:09:04,265 --> 00:09:07,766
Stockholm followed with
a trial and a referendum,

136
00:09:07,846 --> 00:09:12,225
and New York's Manhattan pricing
began only in January 2025 —

137
00:09:12,305 --> 00:09:17,275
thirty years after the paper licence,
twenty-seven after the gantry.

138
00:09:17,275 --> 00:09:21,143
The two systems are designed
as a pair, and the LTA

139
00:09:21,223 --> 00:09:25,013
says so in as many words:
the Vehicle Quota System

140
00:09:25,093 --> 00:09:29,350
"regulates vehicle ownership,
while ERP manages usage".

141
00:09:29,350 --> 00:09:34,025
One caps the stock of cars; the
other prices the flow of them.

142
00:09:34,025 --> 00:09:38,550
And the two levers are traded
against each other in the open.

143
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:42,079
When ERP arrived and congestion eased,

144
00:09:42,159 --> 00:09:47,207
the government released some
10,500 extra COEs between

145
00:09:47,287 --> 00:09:51,275
1997 and 2003 beyond the growth allowance.

146
00:09:51,275 --> 00:09:56,373
In October 2024 the same logic
ran again: up to 20,000 additional

147
00:09:56,453 --> 00:10:00,116
certificates were announced
from February 2025,

148
00:10:00,196 --> 00:10:07,206
justified in part by the better usage management
expected from ERP's satellite successor,

149
00:10:07,286 --> 00:10:10,950
even as the growth rate
itself stayed at zero.

150
00:10:10,950 --> 00:10:14,842
As the transport minister
put it in Parliament in 2023,

151
00:10:14,922 --> 00:10:18,164
the vehicle population
cannot keep increasing,

152
00:10:18,244 --> 00:10:23,003
because the alternatives are to
set aside ever more land for roads,

153
00:10:23,083 --> 00:10:26,550
or to accept the congestion
of other big cities.

154
00:10:26,550 --> 00:10:30,175
Roads already take about
an eighth of the island.

155
00:10:30,175 --> 00:10:34,859
The satellite system also makes a third
possibility technically available —

156
00:10:34,939 --> 00:10:37,781
charging by distance
travelled, rather than at

157
00:10:37,861 --> 00:10:41,846
fixed points — and the government
has been careful to say it has

158
00:10:41,926 --> 00:10:46,102
not decided to use it: there are,
in its words, no immediate plans,

159
00:10:46,182 --> 00:10:49,675
and the launch changes the
hardware, not the framework.

160
00:10:49,675 --> 00:10:52,695
The result is the most expensive place in

161
00:10:52,775 --> 00:10:55,875
the world to buy a car, by a wide margin.

162
00:10:55,875 --> 00:11:01,103
A Toyota Corolla-class car
that costs about 26,300 US

163
00:11:01,183 --> 00:11:06,411
dollars in the United States
costs roughly 156,800 US

164
00:11:06,491 --> 00:11:12,200
dollars in Singapore; the next
dearest city is not close.

165
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:16,505
A worked example from
late 2025: a Corolla Altis

166
00:11:16,585 --> 00:11:20,799
at about 173,000 Singapore
dollars divides into

167
00:11:20,879 --> 00:11:26,646
roughly 25,000 Singapore dollars
of the car's open-market value,

168
00:11:26,726 --> 00:11:30,940
40,000 Singapore dollars
of registration taxes,

169
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:34,400
and 109,000 Singapore dollars of COE.

170
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:38,066
The money is not trivial
to the state either —

171
00:11:38,146 --> 00:11:44,908
quota premiums brought in 4.66 billion
Singapore dollars in the 2023 financial year,

172
00:11:44,988 --> 00:11:50,200
alongside 2.60 billion Singapore
dollars in motor vehicle taxes.

173
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:54,626
The criticisms are longstanding and
are aired in Parliament regularly:

174
00:11:54,706 --> 00:11:57,522
that the system rations
road space by wealth,

175
00:11:57,602 --> 00:12:01,192
that a certificate can cost
more than the car it permits,

176
00:12:01,272 --> 00:12:04,539
that premiums swinging
40,000 Singapore dollars in a

177
00:12:04,619 --> 00:12:08,208
fortnight make planning
impossible, and that private-hire

178
00:12:08,288 --> 00:12:12,150
fleets bidding in the same pool
push prices up for families.

179
00:12:12,150 --> 00:12:16,883
The replies are also on the record:
that the practical alternative

180
00:12:16,963 --> 00:12:21,623
to pricing is rationing by congestion
or by queue; that rates and

181
00:12:21,703 --> 00:12:25,998
quotas follow measured speeds
and land, not revenue targets;

182
00:12:26,078 --> 00:12:31,176
that residents took 84 per cent of
successful car COE bids between 2022

183
00:12:31,256 --> 00:12:35,850
and late 2024; and that supply
smoothing now tempers the cycle.

184
00:12:35,850 --> 00:12:40,472
The newest attempt to adjust the
balance came in October 2026,

185
00:12:40,552 --> 00:12:44,870
when the LTA proposed merging
Categories A and B into one,

186
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:49,724
with a value-based rebate or
surcharge of up to 15,000 Singapore

187
00:12:49,804 --> 00:12:53,975
dollars so that expensive
cars pay more of the premium.

188
00:12:53,975 --> 00:12:58,437
Consultation closed on
the 2nd of November 2026;

189
00:12:58,517 --> 00:13:01,450
the outcome is still undecided.

190
00:13:01,450 --> 00:13:06,000
No study we could find measures
whether ERP charges change where

191
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:10,413
people choose to live; the
research on housing choices points

192
00:13:10,493 --> 00:13:15,050
to the MRT, to schools, to the
distance to work and to parents.

193
00:13:15,050 --> 00:13:19,666
But charges do not need a study to
reach into a family's decisions,

194
00:13:19,746 --> 00:13:22,900
and in one family the
writer knows, they did.

195
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:26,363
Two years ago, visiting
Singapore, I caught up with

196
00:13:26,443 --> 00:13:29,905
a widower who lives in a
landed estate in the north

197
00:13:29,985 --> 00:13:33,250
of the island, a long
way from the city centre.

198
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:36,950
When his wife was alive
the big house was full.

199
00:13:36,950 --> 00:13:40,479
After she died, their son
left for a career in Europe,

200
00:13:40,559 --> 00:13:44,021
and their daughter built
her own career in Singapore;

201
00:13:44,101 --> 00:13:47,175
the house stands mostly
empty, with him in it.

202
00:13:47,175 --> 00:13:51,275
The daughter had at first thought
she would live with her father.

203
00:13:51,275 --> 00:13:54,892
Then she did the sums on the
daily drive — the long run

204
00:13:54,972 --> 00:13:59,127
in to work, down the Central
Expressway and under its gantries,

205
00:13:59,207 --> 00:14:02,488
twice a day — and found
it cheaper to rent a place

206
00:14:02,568 --> 00:14:06,400
of her own, chosen so that no
long daily drive is needed.

207
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:10,425
The family home was there,
and hers for the living in.

208
00:14:10,425 --> 00:14:13,725
The price of using the road outweighed it.

209
00:14:13,725 --> 00:14:18,290
That is the second lever working
at a scale no statistic captures:

210
00:14:18,370 --> 00:14:22,100
not deciding whether she
drives, but where she lives.

211
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:24,845
The gantry network is over twenty-five

212
00:14:24,925 --> 00:14:27,675
years old and at the end of its life.

213
00:14:27,675 --> 00:14:31,940
Its satellite successor has been
in preparation for a decade:

214
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:36,284
studied since about 2013,
contracted in February 2016 for 556

215
00:14:36,364 --> 00:14:42,054
million Singapore dollars to a consortium
of NCS and Mitsubishi Heavy Industries,

216
00:14:42,134 --> 00:14:45,116
and fitted to the fleet
from November 2023,

217
00:14:45,196 --> 00:14:48,891
after the first public
showing of its on-board unit —

218
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:55,301
a three-piece set for cars, with a processing
unit, an antenna and a touchscreen display —

219
00:14:55,381 --> 00:14:58,800
drew sharp public criticism
of its bulk in 2020.

220
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:03,306
Fitting took the design as it was
but answered the loudest complaint,

221
00:15:03,386 --> 00:15:05,500
drivers reaching across to a card

222
00:15:05,580 --> 00:15:09,355
unit in the passenger footwell,
with a choice of placement

223
00:15:09,435 --> 00:15:12,625
and a button to deactivate
the card for parking.

224
00:15:12,625 --> 00:15:16,678
By late 2026 more than
98 per cent of eligible

225
00:15:16,758 --> 00:15:20,631
vehicles carried the
new unit, and every new

226
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:24,575
vehicle has come
pre-fitted since May 2024.

227
00:15:24,575 --> 00:15:27,875
So the frames come down in two waves.

228
00:15:27,875 --> 00:15:31,633
The 62 gantries that no
longer charge went first,

229
00:15:31,713 --> 00:15:35,862
from October 2026 — among
the early removals CNA named

230
00:15:35,942 --> 00:15:40,326
were Bencoolen Street, Geylang
Bahru, Republic Boulevard,

231
00:15:40,406 --> 00:15:44,400
the Kallang–Paya Lebar
Expressway and Dunearn Road.

232
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:48,461
The 33 still working stand until charging

233
00:15:48,541 --> 00:15:51,975
ends on the 31st of December 2026.

234
00:15:51,975 --> 00:15:55,948
By June 2027 all 95 will
be removed or modified,

235
00:15:56,028 --> 00:15:59,664
a few frames kept
standing as masts carrying

236
00:15:59,744 --> 00:16:04,050
support equipment where
satellite signals are weak.

237
00:16:04,050 --> 00:16:08,125
In their place on the road:
an oval blue "ERP" symbol

238
00:16:08,205 --> 00:16:12,125
painted on each lane, and
"ERP Charge Zone" signs.

239
00:16:12,125 --> 00:16:16,201
The on-board unit warns the
driver before a charging point,

240
00:16:16,281 --> 00:16:19,450
shows the charge, and
confirms it afterwards.

241
00:16:19,450 --> 00:16:24,646
The NETS CashCard, the card in every
in-vehicle unit since the 1990s,

242
00:16:24,726 --> 00:16:28,550
stops working on the same
day the old system does.

243
00:16:28,550 --> 00:16:34,327
On the 1st of January 2027, charging by
satellite begins at the same locations,

244
00:16:34,407 --> 00:16:38,479
at rates under the same
framework — the first adjustment

245
00:16:38,559 --> 00:16:43,002
of the new era is a 1 Singapore
dollars rise at two locations

246
00:16:43,082 --> 00:16:47,975
on the Central and Pan-Island
Expressways from the 4th of January.

247
00:16:47,975 --> 00:16:51,050
Nothing about the two levers changes.

248
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:55,409
Only the furniture does: a
generation of drivers who steered

249
00:16:55,489 --> 00:17:00,150
by the gantry's beep will steer
by a painted blue oval instead.

250
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:02,473
Where it fits in the bigger story:

251
00:17:02,553 --> 00:17:06,432
Singapore's answer to an
island that ran out of road was

252
00:17:06,512 --> 00:17:09,975
never to ban the car, nor
to let the jams decide.

253
00:17:09,975 --> 00:17:14,501
It was to price both halves of driving
— a certificate for the owning,

254
00:17:14,581 --> 00:17:17,790
a charge for the using —
and to keep adjusting the

255
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:21,804
pair against each other for
fifty years, from a paper licence

256
00:17:21,884 --> 00:17:25,700
checked by eye to a satellite
that needs no gantry at all.

257
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:28,425
The hardware keeps retiring.

258
00:17:28,425 --> 00:17:30,775
The arithmetic doesn't.
